# Auth API Test Script

## Test the authentication endpoints

### 1. Register a new user
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@iptv4ever.com",
  "name": "Test User",
  "password": "TestP@ss123"
}

###

### 2. Register another user
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@iptv4ever.com",
  "name": "Admin User",
  "password": "AdminP@ss123"
}

###

### 3. Login with first user
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@iptv4ever.com",
  "password": "TestP@ss123"
}

###

### 4. Get user profile (replace TOKEN with actual token from login)
GET http://localhost:5001/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN

###

### 5. Get current user info
GET http://localhost:5001/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN

###

### 6. Get all users (development only)
GET http://localhost:5001/auth/users

###

### 7. Test invalid login
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@iptv4ever.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword"
}

###

### 8. Test duplicate registration
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@iptv4ever.com",
  "name": "Duplicate User",
  "password": "TestP@ss123"
}

###

### 9. Test weak password validation
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "weak@iptv4ever.com",
  "name": "Weak Password User",
  "password": "weak"
}

###

### 10. Test invalid email
POST http://localhost:5001/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "invalid-email",
  "name": "Invalid Email User",
  "password": "ValidP@ss123"
}

###
